    proseHtml:
      "<p class=\"lead\">After-hours delivery moves your freight outside normal business hours, and time-slot delivery lands it inside a booked window at the receiver's site. Road Linx Transport runs both across Brisbane and South East Queensland, for the many deliveries that can't just turn up whenever a truck happens to be free.</p><p>If your freight has to arrive before a store opens, land in a booked dock slot, or move overnight to dodge traffic and downtime, this is the service built for it.</p><h2>Why timing is its own service</h2><p>Plenty of receivers won't accept freight outside a set window. Distribution centres run booked dock slots and turn trucks away that miss them. Retailers want stock in before customers arrive. Building sites need materials before the crew starts. Get the timing wrong and the delivery fails, even though the freight was ready and the truck turned up.</p><p>Treating delivery timing as a planned part of the job, not an afterthought, is what stops those failures.</p><h2>Time-slot deliveries to DCs and retailers</h2><p>Distribution centres often issue a delivery window and expect the truck in that window, no earlier and no later. Missing it can mean a rejected load, a rebooking days later, or a penalty.</p><p>We plan runs around booked slots so the truck is there on time, loaded correctly for a fast unload. Our drivers know how DC receiving works, so your freight moves through their gate cleanly instead of getting bogged down. Hitting the slot reliably is what keeps you in good standing with the receiver.</p><h2>Early morning and late night runs</h2><p>Some deliveries are simply better done when the roads are quiet and the business is closed.</p><h2>Early morning</h2><p>Stock delivered before opening means shelves are full when customers walk in and staff aren't unloading during trade. It also beats the worst of the traffic, so the run is quicker and more predictable.</p><h2>Late night and overnight</h2><p>Overnight delivery suits sites that can't take freight during the day, and it's the backbone of warehouse moves and restocks that have to happen while a business is closed. You open the next morning already sorted.</p><h2>Avoiding congestion and penalties</h2><p>After-hours running isn't only about receiver rules. Moving freight outside peak traffic means fewer delays, tighter timing and lower risk of missing a downstream commitment. For time-critical supply, that predictability is worth as much as the delivery itself.</p><h2>How we run timed deliveries</h2><ul><li>Tell us the delivery window or the after-hours timing the receiver needs.</li><li>We plan the run and the load so the truck arrives on time and unloads fast.</li><li>We deliver in the window, tracked, with a POD to prove it landed on time.</li><li>For ongoing timed runs, we lock it in as a standing arrangement.</li></ul><p>Whether it's a one-off booked slot or a nightly restock, the aim is the same. Your freight arrives exactly when it's meant to, and never a delivery that bounces because it showed up at the wrong time.</p><h2>Why on-time carriers get looked after</h2><p>Distribution centres keep score. Carriers who hit their booked slots consistently get smoother access, better bookings and fewer problems at the gate. Carriers who turn up late get pushed to the back or turned away.</p><p>When we run your timed deliveries, we're protecting that standing on your behalf. A load that lands in its window, ready for a fast unload, keeps you in the good books with the receiver and avoids the penalties and rebooking fees that a missed slot brings. Over time that reliability is worth more than the freight rate itself.</p><p>From pre-dawn retail drops to late-night restocks and booked weekend windows, the timing is the service. Tell us the hour the freight has to land and we build the run backwards from it.</p>",
