    proseHtml:
      "<p class=\"lead\">General freight transport is the day-to-day movement of palletised and non-palletised goods between businesses, warehouses and job sites. Road Linx Transport handles that everyday freight across Brisbane, the Port of Brisbane and the wider South East Queensland corridor, with trucks sized from one-tonne utes through to 24-pallet semi-trailers.</p><p>If you need a dependable freight company in Brisbane that turns up when it says it will and gets your load there in one piece, this is the service that covers most of what you send.</p><h2>What we move as general freight</h2><p>General freight is a broad category, and that's the point. Most business freight fits here without needing a specialist service. We regularly carry:</p><ul><li>Palletised stock, from a single pallet to a full trailer load</li><li>Cartons, crates, drums and shrink-wrapped goods</li><li>Building and trade materials heading to sites</li><li>Retail and wholesale stock moving between distribution centres and stores</li><li>Machinery, fittings and awkward items that still sit within a standard trailer</li></ul><p>If your freight is oversize, needs a flat deck, or has to be lifted at a site with no forklift, we'll point you to the right trailer instead. That's usually a flatbed, a drop deck or a tail-lift truck, and we run all three.</p><h2>Why businesses pick Road Linx for freight</h2><p>Reliability is the whole job. A late pallet can hold up a production line or leave a customer standing at a loading dock, so we plan runs around your window, not ours.</p><h2>Load-rated equipment, quicker turnarounds</h2><p>Our trailers run load-rated restraint gear as standard. That means loads are secured to the rating printed on the equipment, so we're not improvising with whatever straps are in the cab. It keeps your freight stable and it keeps our loading and unloading times short, which is part of why our turnaround tends to beat operators still using general-purpose gear.</p><h2>Drivers who know load restraint</h2><p>Every driver is trained in load restraint and works to Chain of Responsibility obligations. If a load isn't safe to move, it doesn't move until it is. You get freight that arrives undamaged and a business that isn't exposed to a compliance problem further up the chain.</p><h2>Local Brisbane freight and the wider region</h2><p>Plenty of our work is short-haul metro freight inside Brisbane and out to the Port. We also run regular freight south to the Gold Coast and Tweed, west to Toowoomba and the Darling Downs, and north through the Sunshine Coast to the Wide Bay.</p><p>Because we cover the region ourselves rather than handing your freight to a third party, there's no depot-to-depot double handling in the middle. Your goods stay on our truck from pickup to delivery, which is faster and far kinder to fragile stock.</p><h2>How booking freight works</h2><ul><li>Tell us the pickup and delivery addresses, what you're sending and when it needs to land.</li><li>We match the right truck and trailer to the load and confirm a price.</li><li>We collect, secure the freight to rating, and track it through to delivery.</li><li>You get confirmation on delivery, and a signed paper POD if you need one for your records.</li></ul><h2>Freight that fits your schedule</h2><p>Not every load can move at 10am on a Tuesday. We run early morning starts, after-hours runs and short-notice pickups for freight that has to move around a business's real operating hours. If a regular driver is off sick or on leave and your freight still needs to go, we can cover that gap too.</p><p>For ongoing senders we can set up standing runs, so the same freight moves on the same days without a fresh booking each time.</p><h2>A freight partner, not just a truck for the day</h2><p>There's a difference between ringing around for whoever's cheapest this week and having a freight company that knows your business. When the same carrier handles your freight run after run, they learn your sites, your customers and the way you like things done.</p><p>That familiarity is worth real money. Fewer failed deliveries because the driver knows the tricky loading dock. Faster bookings because we already have your details. And one point of accountability when something needs sorting, instead of a shrug and a claim form. For businesses that send freight regularly, that consistency usually beats chasing the lowest quote every time.</p>",
    proseStyle: null,
