    proseHtml:
      "<p class=\"lead\">A taxi truck is exactly what it sounds like. You book a truck for a single job, it turns up, moves your load, and you pay for that trip rather than a full-day or ongoing rate. Road Linx Transport runs taxi trucks across Brisbane in sizes from one-tonne utes up to 12-tonne trucks, so you can get one item or a few pallets moved without hiring a truck by the day.</p><p>It's the quickest way to shift freight that's too big for a courier and too small to justify a full load.</p><h2>When a taxi truck is the right call</h2><p>Taxi trucks fill the awkward middle ground between a parcel courier and a booked freight run. You'll reach for one when:</p><ul><li>A pallet or two has to get across town today</li><li>A courier ute is too small but a semi-trailer is overkill</li><li>You've got a one-off delivery and don't want an account or a schedule</li><li>Something has been left off a load and needs to catch up</li><li>A customer needs stock now and can't wait for the next scheduled run</li><li>Because you're paying for the job and not the day, it's cost-effective for exactly this kind of ad-hoc work.</li></ul><h2>Pick the right size truck</h2><p>Sending the wrong size truck wastes money either way, so we size it to the load.</p><h2>One-tonne utes and utes</h2><p>For a handful of cartons, a single pallet or small items, a ute or flat-top ute does the job quickly and cheaply. This is the go-to for light, urgent runs around the metro.</p><h2>Three to twelve-tonne trucks</h2><p>When the load grows to several pallets or heavier gear, we step up to a mid-size or larger truck. Many of these carry a tail lift, so we can still deliver to sites without a forklift.</p><h2>Fast dispatch across the metro</h2><p>The value of a taxi truck is speed, so we keep vehicles moving around Brisbane and the Port ready to pick up. For local runs we can often have a truck to you the same day, and for genuinely urgent jobs our hot shot service runs a dedicated dash straight there.</p><p>You get a driver who knows the metro, load-rated restraint so your goods travel safely, and a signed POD on delivery if you need the paperwork.</p><h2>No account, no fuss</h2><p>You don't need an ongoing arrangement to use a taxi truck. Plenty of our taxi truck jobs are one-offs for businesses that usually run their own vehicles but have hit a busy day, a breakdown or an extra order. Call it in, we quote the trip, and it's done.</p><p>If you find you're booking taxi trucks often, we can set you up with an account or move you onto a standing run, whichever works out better for you.</p><h2>Booking a taxi truck</h2><ul><li>Tell us what you're moving, from where to where, and when.</li><li>We size the truck and quote the trip.</li><li>The truck is dispatched, loads, and delivers direct.</li><li>You get a POD on request. No day rate, no ongoing commitment.</li></ul><h2>When to switch from taxi trucks to an account</h2><p>A taxi truck is perfect for the odd job, but there's a point where booking them one by one stops making sense. If you're calling for a truck two or three times a week, you're doing more admin than you need to and probably not getting the best rate.</p><p>That's the moment to talk about an account or a standing run. You keep the on-demand flexibility for genuine one-offs, but your regular movements get set up once and priced better. We'll be upfront about it. If a regular arrangement would save you money over ad-hoc taxi trucks, we'll say so.</p>",
